00:00:00,670 --> 00:00:03,030
(Transcribed by TurboScribe. Go Unlimited to remove this message.) Madison recently got her driver's license.

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:04,630
She is happy.

3
00:00:05,410 --> 00:00:07,150
She has a lot of freedom now.

4
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:09,310
She can go anywhere.

5
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:12,450
She doesn't have to walk to school anymore.

6
00:00:13,110 --> 00:00:15,309
She can drive to her friend's house.

7
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:19,090
Madison has a younger sister named Lisa.

8
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:23,330
Lisa is 14 and has school at 8

9
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,230
o'clock in the morning.

10
00:00:25,190 --> 00:00:28,270
Madison's parents asked her to drive Lisa to

11
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:29,510
school every morning.

12
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,490
Why do I have to wake up?

13
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:33,950
Madison asked.

14
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:38,770
Having a license means having more responsibilities, her

15
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:39,610
mom replied.

16
00:00:40,430 --> 00:00:42,930
Her parents also asked her to pick up

17
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:43,350
groceries.

18
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:47,430
Madison did not like having a license anymore.
